BRXSRCHT                                                         MAINTC command

Use the BRXSRCHT command to setup a minidisk search order to build and
modify a test version of the bREXX code.

The format of the BRXSRCHT command is:
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| BRXSRCHT |                                                                  |
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Usage Notes:

1. The minidisk search order after issuing this command is:

   MNT191  191  A    R/W     Work disk where compiled code is created
   MNT493  493  B/A  R/O     Files for test bREXX version
   MNT193  193  E/A  R/O     TEXT files for the compiled bREXX code
   MNT393  393  F/A  R/O     bREXX source code
   MNT394  394  G/A  R/O     GCC H files for CMS specific runtime
   MNT194  194  H/A  R/O     GCCLIB MACLIB for compiled bREXX code
